---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import photoFounder from '../assets/photos/founder.jpg';

const founding = await getEntry('stories', 'founding-story');
---
<BaseLayout title="About Pozole | MyPozole" description="The real history of pozole, the three styles, what's actually in the toppings, and how MyPozole started.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="label">About Pozole</p>
      <h1>A dish older than the country it comes from.</h1>
    </header>

    <section class="history">
      <p>
        Pozole's name comes from the Nahuatl word <em>pozolli</em>, meaning
        foamy or frothy, a reference to how the corn looks as it cooks down
        into hominy. The dish itself predates the Spanish arrival in Mexico
        by centuries, eaten across Mesoamerica under Aztec rule as early as
        the 1300s. Corn wasn't just food to the Aztecs, it was sacred, tied
        directly to their origin stories, and pozole was reserved for
        ceremonial occasions rather than eaten as an everyday meal.
      </p>
      <p>
        In this family, it starts with big cuts of pork, browned first,
        then simmered low until tender enough to pull apart by hand. That
        broth is what the hominy simmers in, the same order Jorge learned
        making it alongside his mother. Simple ingredients, done in the
        right order, is most of what makes it taste like a family recipe
        instead of a restaurant dish. Over the generations, cooks across
        Mexico's regions built their own variations on that same hominy
        base, and today those variations have settled into three
        recognized styles: White, Red, and Green.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="styles">
      <div class="style-card">
        <h3>White <span class="es">(Blanco)</span></h3>
        <p>The base recipe, hominy and broth, built for everyone to finish their own way at the table. This is the style Jorge's family has made for generations, from Mexico City.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="style-card">
        <h3>Red <span class="es">(Rojo)</span></h3>
        <p>Made with guajillo chiles. Carries 50% of the daily value of Vitamin A across all three proteins. The red salsa on the side does not carry real heat, that comes from chile flakes, added separately.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="style-card">
        <h3>Green <span class="es">(Verde)</span></h3>
        <p>Made with tomatillos and serrano peppers, the serranos are the actual chile, tomatillos are their own fruit, not a pepper. Meaningfully more Vitamin C than the other two. Unlike the red salsa, the green salsa does carry real heat, from those same serranos.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="story">
      <div class="story-photo">
        <Image src={photoFounder} alt="Jorge, MyPozole's founder, topping a cup at the farmers market" width={480} height={270} />
      </div>
      <h2>How MyPozole started</h2>
      {founding?.data.body ? (
        founding.data.body.split('\n\n').map((para) => <p>{para}</p>)
      ) : (
        <p class="pending">This section is still being written, sourced from three published pieces about MyPozole. Coming soon.</p>
      )}
    </section>

    <nav class="cross-links">
      <a href="/menu">See the menu →</a>
      <a href="/where-to-buy">Where to buy →</a>
      <a href="/catering/home">Catering →</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head { padding: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-3); }
  .page-head h1 { max-width: 18ch; }

  .history { padding-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .history p { font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.7; opacity: 0.82; max-width: 68ch; margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .history em { font-style: italic; color: var(--rust); font-weight: 600; }

  .styles { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--space-2); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .styles { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .style-card { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; padding: var(--space-3); background: var(--paper); }
  .style-card h3 { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .es { font-weight: 500; opacity: 0.55; font-size: 0.7em; }
  .style-card p { font-size: 14.5px; opacity: 0.76; line-height: 1.6; }

  .story { padding: var(--space-4) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft); }
  .story-photo { aspect-ratio: 16/9; max-width: 480px; border-radius: 4px; background: var(--sand-pale); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); overflow: hidden; }
  .story-photo img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
  .story h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .story p { font-size: 16px; opacity: 0.8; max-width: 62ch; line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .pending { opacity: 0.55; font-style: italic; }

  .cross-links { display: flex; gap: var(--space-3); padding: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-6); flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .cross-links a { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--terracotta); text-decoration: none; }
  .cross-links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
